# Packages only the arm64 live image needs. build.sh copies this file into the package
# lists; live-build adds the kernel itself (--linux-flavours). The image targets machines
# that boot a generic UEFI Debian; boards that need their own firmware are devices/.
# Secure Boot: Debian's signed shim and GRUB, installed into the target by Calamares, and
# grub-efi-arm64, whose maintainer scripts put GRUB's updates on the ESP.
grub-efi-arm64
grub-efi-arm64-signed
shim-signed
# The initramfs tool Debian 13 uses: the backports kernel takes dracut as well, and the
# live system and the installer's initramfs step are made for this one.
initramfs-tools
# The firmware of the Snapdragon X Elite laptops the boot menu has entries for
# (devices/snapdragon-x-elite/, extra_packages; its wifi's is in the common list): the
# battery, the USB-C ports and the graphics start only with it, and the installed
# system has it from its first start. Debian 13's own package, 93 MB.
firmware-qcom-soc
